    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d74">

                <pb facs="0213" n="155" xml:id="pg155"/>

                <head>Señor Romero to Mr.
                        Seward</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Mexican Legation in the United States
                                of America</hi>, <hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Washington</hi>,</placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1866-05-26"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >May</hi> 26, 1866.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Secretary:</hi> In conformity with the promise I
                    made in my interview with you in the State Department this morning, I have the
                    honor to enclose the copy of a communication<anchor n="*" xml:id="d74-f1"/>
                    addressed to me, on the 21st instant, from Elizabeth-port, by Don Antonio Lopez
                    de Santa Anna, in which he offers his services to the Mexican government, and my
                    answer* to it of yesterday, informing him that I was not authorized to consider
                    the proposal, but would submit it to my government.</p>
                <p>Your respectful and obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>M. ROMERO.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">William H. Seward</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d74-f1" n="*" xml:id="d74-f1-content">
                <p>For enclosures see enclosures Nos. 5 and 7 to Señor Romero’s note of the 12th of
                    August.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
